  "name": "fmodel-rust-postgres",
  "description": "A comprehensive template and framework for developing PostgreSQL extensions in Rust that implement tactical Domain-Driven Design patterns. It leverages the fmodel-rust library to execute complex domain logic—including aggregates, sagas, and materialized views—directly within the database engine via the pgrx framework. This architecture facilitates high-performance event sourcing and CQRS by embedding state evolution and event persistence logic within the RDBMS runtime.",
